# ============================================================================
# xlayer_short.buda — cross-trunk-layer corner-overlap → detailed-NUTS stub short
# ============================================================================
# Standalone repro for the detailed-NUTS cross-layer spacing fix
# (see docs/future/nuts_packing_gaps.md §3, PR #12).
#
# Setup: three TOP layers, with M4 and M6 sharing the SAME origin (-400) and
# pattern, so their signal tracks are ALIGNED.  Two buses are pinned to Z-topos
# whose first V-stubs share the x≈90 column (u1 and u3).  The sidecar
# xlayer_short.json pins bus x's H-trunk to M4; bus y's trunk defaults to M6 —
# so the two trunks are on DIFFERENT layers (the cross-trunk-layer case), both
# wanting y≈125.
#
# WHAT TO OBSERVE
#   Old build (before the carry-bound fix): abstract NUTS separates the trunks
#   only by g=1, then detailed NUTS snaps each to its own layer's nearest signal
#   track INDEPENDENTLY.  Because M4/M6 are aligned, both land on the same
#   coordinate, so the two M5 stubs (x's V1a and y's V2a) end up on the SAME M5
#   tracks with OVERLAPPING y-spans — a bit-level short that DetailedNUTS does
#   not report ("0 bits unplaced").  Inspect with tools/show_detailed_shorts.py.
#
#   Fixed build: the abstract per-trunk split bound is carried into detailed
#   NUTS, which filters each trunk's signal tracks to its bounded side.  The
#   trunks land on DISJOINT real tracks (M4 below, M6 above), the stub y-spans
#   become disjoint, and the short is gone (0 shorts, 0 unplaced).
#
# Run:
#   cd src && python3 buda_cli.py ../flow/xlayer_short.buda --no-viz
#   python3 tools/show_detailed_shorts.py flow/xlayer_short.buda   # from repo root
#
# NOTE: requires the co-located sidecar xlayer_short.json (it pins bus x's trunk
# to M4 — there is no .buda command to pin a segment's layer inline).
# ============================================================================

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 52.94
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 50.00
def_layer 6 M6 H TOP 52.94
def_track_pattern 4 -400  POWER 4 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  GROUND 4 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1
def_track_pattern 5    0  POWER 3 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  GROUND 3 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1
def_track_pattern 6 -400  POWER 4 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1 SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  GROUND 4 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1  SIGNAL 2 1

add_block u1    80   50   100 100
add_block u2    150  50   200 100
add_block u3    80  150   100 200
add_block u4    175 150   225 200

add_bus x[4]  u1.o u4.i
add_bus y[4]  u3.o u2.i

run_bundler strict

corner_margin dy 2 dx 2
set_min_stub_length 2
generate_topologies
check_design topo

# Pin both Z-topos; the sidecar (xlayer_short.json) puts bus x's trunk on M4.
select_topologies 1,2 4
run_planner 1

run_nuts
check_design nuts
run_detailed_nuts
check_design dnuts

visualize
